            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A cassette configured for installation in a fiber enclosure system, the cassette comprising: a base, a first side wall including a first notch; a second side wall including a second notch, the second side wall being opposite the first side wall; a front wall with an opening including an adapter configured to connect to at least one fiber optic cable; a latch including a through opening, the latch configured to extend through the first notch opening of the first side wall and releasably connect the cassette to a rail included in the fiber enclosure system; and a lock disposed within the cassette, wherein the lock is configured to actuate the latch into an unlocked position by disconnecting the latch from the rail and actuate the latch into a locked position by connecting the latch to the rail, wherein the lock includes a retraction mechanism including an arm configured to fit through the through opening of the latch.</p>
            </abstract>
